            <p>
               <l>NEW YEAR'S PARTY 1979</l>
               <l>…New Year’s Eve in Seattle saw one of the most</l><l>all around <hi rend="ul"
                     >amusing</hi> parties in years--local</l>
               <l>freaks packed the enemy’s practice studio</l>
               <l>to down Guyana punch + dance their hearts</l>
               <l>away to the <hi rend="ul">way out sounds</hi> of the Radio’s,</l>
               <l>The St. Bernard Quartet, The Girls, The Enemy,</l>
               <l>The Fishsticks, The Mystery Horns, not to</l>
               <l>mention an outstanding display of charisma by</l>
               <l>George “Johnny Ray” Gleason + The Boppin’ Sounds</l>
               <l>of Rick “Buddy Holly” Smith…Lots more bands but</l>
               <l>we can't remember ‘em all (Cheaters? Electric Tramps?)</l>
               <l>...Tons of fun…stupid hats, champagne, noisemakers</l>
               <l>+ <hi rend="ul">Everything</hi>! <hi rend="ul">Wow</hi>! (A nite to remember</l>
               <l>fo’ sho’!!)</l></p>

            <p>! -> <hi rend="ul">Photos L to R from top:</hi></p>

            <p>Rick Smith + Nina</p>

            <p>Mystery Horns Homer, Roland, + Edward Cardboard</p>

            <p>Mass Hysteria</p>

            <p>Fishsticks (World Premiere!)</p>

            <p>Tammy Smith</p>

            <p>The Enemy (Suzy + George)</p>

            <p>Gregor Gayden (St. Bernard Qt.)</p>

            <p>George… “If your Heartaches..!”</p>

            <p>Bob Kondraic w/Cambea</p>

            <p>More Hysteria (Yahoo! Yreka!)</p>

            <p>Damon (?) Titus</p>

            <p>Don Harper, Er. So on– –<hi rend="ul">Deeyow</hi>!!</p>

            <p>(Sorry if we forgot ya!)</p>

            <p><hi rend="ul">Photos</hi>: Randy Hall</p>
